This is a scoped TypeScript adaptation, not the complete perms filter. It is
the identity on frames: frames here carry no writability flag, so each input
frame is forwarded without a copy or allocation. It refuses mode=random without
an explicit seed (native draws one from av_get_random_seed), numeric and
expression mode values, seeds outside canonical decimal, the generic timeline
option enable, the generic threads option and runtime commands, and adds no
FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
